      "updated_at": "2018-10-25T20:20:57Z",
      "body": "From an administrators point of view being able to change the access or directly access/simulate access to a user account without his consent is questionable in many ways. (in so far as the user is not part of your own team/company - and even this could be tricky sometimes). \r\n\r\nSo as a member of the european privacy protection act, I have to be completely against such a feature, because it would render the software unusable for us. ",
      "author_association": "NONE",
