      "created_at": "2018-10-26T16:15:04Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-10-26T16:15:04Z",
      "body": "I was able to recover the password while it was not even verified, it seems it's working correctly.\r\n@Mte90 Please make sure the user has its account verified. It should show a warning on its profile if it's not.\r\n![screenshot](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6447076/47578320-79793400-d91f-11e8-809c-7faec0923626.png)\r\nYou can manually verify an user on the database by changing the `verification_token` row on `ticket` table to `NULL`.\r\nIf the email is not verified, the user will not be able to log in and a message `Email is not verified` will appear. I'm thinking we should maybe add a \"resend verification email\" button like other websites do, because currently it's only sent once.\r\n\r\nEven if we're talking about users without expertise. Email verification it's still necessary because we need to very the authenticity of the email, of course this won't be always needed when we implement #207.",
